IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea89-types`
IMPORT `ea89-days`
IMPORT `ea89-connection`
IMPORT `ea89-nonpayment`
IMPORT `ea89-redress`

-- Electricity Act 1989 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Seat: the electricity
-- customer.
--
--   "Must the distributor connect my premises, or keep them connected; when
--    can it disconnect me; what interest is due on my security; until when
--    can I refer a dispute? Can my supplier fit a pre-payment meter or
--    disconnect me for debt, from when, and may it enter? And if Ofgem acts
--    on my supplier's breach, can a redress order still be made, by when must
--    I be paid, and what can I recover on electricity resold to me?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Electricity customer case` HAS
    `bank holidays`                                     IS A LIST OF DATE
    `the connection`                                    IS A MAYBE `Connection request`
    `the security deposit`                              IS A MAYBE `Security deposit`
    `the non-payment`                                   IS A MAYBE `Non-payment case`
    `the contravention`                                 IS A MAYBE `Contravention facts`
    `the redress order`                                 IS A MAYBE `Redress order facts`
    `the resale`                                        IS A MAYBE `Resale facts`

DECLARE `Electricity customer position` HAS
    `connection`                                        IS A MAYBE `Connection outcome`
    `earliest disconnection under s 17(1)(c)`           IS A MAYBE DATE
    `last day to refer a connection dispute`            IS A MAYBE DATE
    `interest on my security deposit`                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `earliest day for a pre-payment meter or disconnection` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `supplier may act on the day`                       IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `officer may enter`                                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `restoring it myself is an offence`                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `redress order can be made`                         IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `compliance date is lawful`                         IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `supplier's last day to appeal`                     IS A MAYBE DATE
    `interest on compensation runs from`                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `most compensation for the contravention`           IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `recoverable on resale`                             IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 16-23, 27G-27O, 44, 64(1), Sch 6 paras 2, 5, 7, 8, 10
@export default The electricity customer's position under the Electricity Act 1989 (UK): whether the distributor must connect or keep connected my premises, the earliest day it may disconnect me under s 17(1)(c), the last day to refer a connection dispute (s 23(1C)) and the interest on my security deposit (s 20(3)); from when my supplier may fit a pre-payment meter or disconnect me for unpaid charges, whether it may on the day, whether its officer may enter, and whether restoring the connection myself is an offence (Sch 6 paras 2, 5, 7, 8, 10); whether a consumer redress order can be made for its contravention, whether the order's compliance date is lawful, its last day to appeal, from when interest runs on unpaid compensation, and the most compensation in all (ss 27G-27O); and what I can recover on electricity resold to me above the maximum price (s 44). Working days exclude the bank holidays given. Each is NOTHING where its facts are not given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Electricity customer case`  @desc The bank holidays, the connection request, any security deposit, any non-payment, the contravention and redress order, and any resale
GIVETH A `Electricity customer position`
`the electricity customer position for` c MEANS
    `Electricity customer position` WITH
        `connection`                                    IS
            CONSIDER c's `the connection`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (`must the distributor connect` r)
        `earliest disconnection under s 17(1)(c)`       IS
            CONSIDER c's `the connection`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST r  THEN `the earliest day I can be disconnected under s 17(1)(c) for` r `, bank holidays` hols
        `last day to refer a connection dispute`        IS
            CONSIDER c's `the connection`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST r  THEN `the last day to refer a connection dispute for` r
        `interest on my security deposit`               IS
            CONSIDER c's `the security deposit`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`the interest on my security deposit` s)
        `earliest day for a pre-payment meter or disconnection` IS
            CONSIDER c's `the non-payment`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN `the earliest day for a pre-payment meter or disconnection for` k `, bank holidays` hols
        `supplier may act on the day`                   IS
            CONSIDER c's `the non-payment`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`the supplier may act on the day for` k `, bank holidays` hols)
        `officer may enter`                             IS
            CONSIDER c's `the non-payment`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`the officer may enter for` k `, bank holidays` hols)
        `restoring it myself is an offence`             IS
            CONSIDER c's `the non-payment`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`restoring the connection myself is an offence for` k)
        `redress order can be made`                     IS
            CONSIDER c's `the contravention`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`a consumer redress order can be made for` k)
        `compliance date is lawful`                     IS
            CONSIDER c's `the redress order`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN JUST (`the compliance date is lawful for` o)
        `supplier's last day to appeal`                 IS
            CONSIDER c's `the redress order`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN JUST (`the supplier's last day to appeal for` o)
        `interest on compensation runs from`            IS
            CONSIDER c's `the redress order`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN `interest on my compensation runs from` o
        `most compensation for the contravention`       IS
            CONSIDER c's `the redress order`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN JUST (`the most compensation for the contravention under` o)
        `recoverable on resale`                         IS
            CONSIDER c's `the resale`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`what I can recover on resale under` s)
    WHERE
        hols MEANS c's `bank holidays`
